{# Planned, timed closure (25 Nov 2026, Ian). At 09:05 the Roadworks page
   said Traffic Scotland was reporting no closures on the A78 while the
   road was twenty-five minutes from its daily closure. Both were true:
   the incident feed is unplanned events only. So the planned closure is
   said here, from planned.json, on the Today board and on Roadworks, all
   day and not only once it has started.

   The sentence is true at any hour as written, so it stands with
   JavaScript off. The script changes only the badge, by the Largs clock:
   "Closes 09:30 today" before, "Closed until 15:00" (and red) inside the
   hours, "Closes 09:30 tomorrow" after. These are the operator's
   published hours, not a reading of the road, and the source line says so.

   Amber, like any incident short of a closure; red only inside the hours.
   Same frame as the power-cut, flood and Traffic Scotland notices.

   Two lengths. Roadworks (the page that sets `trunkAll`) carries all of
   it: lights, diversion, where the end date comes from. The Today board
   carries one sentence and a link to Roadworks, because on a phone the
   full text was most of the first screen. #}
{% set plannedLive = planned.closures | currentNotices %}
{% for c in plannedLive %}{% if c.nights %}{% include "planned-nights.njk" %}{% else %}
{# ONE NOTICE, NOT TWO (25 Nov 2026, Ian). Inside the hours Traffic Scotland
   reports this same closure, and the board showed two red boxes saying one
   thing. If this build's feed holds a closure whose sentence names one of
   the places in `match`, it is reported here, with their time and link,
   and trunk-notice.njk leaves its own box out for that event. Their report
   is the live reading, so it also makes this notice red (data-ts) whatever
   the clock says. #}
{% set plannedTs = [] %}
{% if today.trunk and today.trunk.ok %}{% for t in today.trunk.items %}{% if t.closed %}{% for w in (c.match or []) %}{% if (w | lower) in (t.text | lower) and not (plannedTs | length) %}{% set plannedTs = (plannedTs.push(t), plannedTs) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="power-notice planned-notice{% if plannedTs | length %} is-closed{% endif %}" role="status" id="planned-{{ c.id }}"
       data-from="{{ c.closeFrom }}" data-to="{{ c.closeTo }}" data-expires="{{ c.expires }}"{% if plannedTs | length %} data-ts="1"{% endif %}>
    <span class="power-notice-badge">Daily closure</span>
    <span class="power-notice-text">
      {% if trunkAll %}<strong>{{ c.road }}</strong> — closed <span class="mono planned-hours">{{ c.closeFrom }}–{{ c.closeTo }}</span> every day for {{ c.reason }}. {{ c.between }} {{ c.diversion }} {{ c.finish }} · <a href="/buses/">Buses →</a>
      {% else %}<strong>{{ c.road }}</strong> — closed <span class="mono planned-hours">{{ c.closeFrom }}–{{ c.closeTo }}</span> every day for {{ c.reason }}, {{ c.finishShort }} · <a href="/roadworks/">Roadworks →</a> · <a href="/buses/">Buses →</a>{% endif %}
      {% if plannedTs | length %}· Traffic Scotland says it is closed{% if plannedTs[0].whenValue %} · {{ plannedTs[0].whenLabel }} <span class="mono">{{ plannedTs[0].whenValue }}</span>{% endif %} · <a href="https://www.traffic.gov.scot/traffic-information/incidents">Traffic Scotland →</a>{% endif %}
    </span>
    <span class="power-notice-src">{% if plannedTs | length %}Amey’s published hours · Traffic Scotland · checked {{ today.trunk.checkedAt | hhmm }}{% else %}{{ c.source }}{% endif %}</span>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
(function () {
  var el = document.getElementById("planned-{{ c.id }}");
  if (!el) return;
  var badge = el.querySelector(".power-notice-badge");
  var from = el.getAttribute("data-from"), to = el.getAttribute("data-to"), last = el.getAttribute("data-expires");
  function largs() {
    try {
      var d = new Date();
      return {
        time: new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-GB", { timeZone: "Europe/London", hour: "2-digit", minute: "2-digit", hourCycle: "h23" }).format(d),
        day: new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-CA", { timeZone: "Europe/London", year: "numeric", month: "2-digit", day: "2-digit" }).format(d)
      };
    } catch (e) { return null; }
  }
  function tick() {
    var n = largs();
    if (!n || !/^\d\d:\d\d$/.test(n.time) || !/^\d{4}-\d\d-\d\d$/.test(n.day)) return;
    if (n.day > last) { el.hidden = true; return; }
    // Traffic Scotland reporting it closed (data-ts, set by the build)
    // counts as closed whatever the published hours say.
    var ts = el.hasAttribute("data-ts");
    var closed = ts || (n.time >= from && n.time < to);
    // After the hours on the last day there is no closure left to announce.
    if (!ts && n.day === last && n.time >= to) { el.hidden = true; return; }
    el.classList.toggle("is-closed", closed);
    badge.textContent = closed ? (n.time < to ? "Closed until " + to : "Closed")
      : n.time < from ? "Closes " + from + " today"
      : "Closes " + from + " tomorrow";
  }
  tick();
  setInterval(tick, 30000);
})();
</script>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
